// Gegenpress — retention and erasure. NOT part of the bootstrap.
//
// The free ADX cluster this project was verified on rejects policy and
// purge commands ("endpoint does not exist"), so these are kept out of
// 01_schema.kql, where a failure would stop the bootstrap. Run them on a
// paid cluster or a Fabric Eventhouse, as a database admin.

//
// 1. Retention. The Form Line compares a player with his own season, so
//    the store needs this season and the last one -- the first matches of
//    a new season are measured against the previous one. Two seasons is
//    the purpose; nothing older is kept. GDPR Art. 5(1)(e).
//
.alter-merge table Events policy retention softdelete = 730d recoverability = disabled

//
// Reference tables are overwritten wholesale on each season load, so they
// hold no history to expire. Stated so the absence is a decision.
//

//
// 2. Erasure, for a request under GDPR Art. 17 where the deployer has no
//    overriding ground to keep the data. A purge is permanent, needs purge
//    enabled on the cluster and database-admin rights, and runs against
//    the ingest- (data management) endpoint. It is two steps on purpose:
//    the first only counts what would go (NumRecordsToPurge) and returns a
//    verification token; nothing is deleted until the second.
//
//    Replace PLAYER_ID. Afterwards rebuild the season baselines, because
//    his match means were part of the league distribution every other
//    player is compared against.
//
// Step 1 -- count and get a token:
//   .purge table Events records in database gegenpress <| where player_id == "PLAYER_ID"
// Step 2 -- execute with that token:
//   .purge table Events records in database gegenpress with (verificationtoken=h'<token from step 1>') <| where player_id == "PLAYER_ID"
